{"_id":"68a7360f8ec3d8323af135e1","nodeId":"X0CKM9LaJUrgI5gIdqFvU","roadmapSlug":"computer-science","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:54.940Z","description":"# State Machine Diagrams\n\nState machine diagrams are used to show the different states an object can be in at a given time. The object can be in one and only one state at a given time. State machine diagrams are similar to activity diagrams, but they are more focused on the flow of an object's state rather than the flow of the object itself.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is State Machine Diagram?","url":"https://www.visual-paradigm.com/guide/uml-unified-modeling-language/what-is-state-machine-diagram/","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3b45"},{"type":"article","title":"State Machine Diagram Tutorial","url":"https://www.lucidchart.com/pages/uml-state-machine-diagram","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3b46"},{"type":"article","title":"State Machine Diagram","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/state-machine-diagram","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3b47"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:21.077Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/computer-science/content/X0CKM9LaJUrgI5gIdqFvU.md"}